    "md5": "cfa09e867b82cf293c18923aa58b0c6c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1531,
    "chunk_text": "President condemns Iran attacks in call with UAE leader\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake held a telephone conversation with United Arab Emirates (UAE) President Sheikh Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan yesterday, during which he condemned recent Iranian attacks targeting the UAE and several Arab countries.\n\nAccording to the UAE\u2019s official news agency WAM, President Dissanayake also conveyed Sri Lanka\u2019s support for the UAE in safeguarding its sovereignty, security, territorial integrity, and the safety of its citizens.\n\nSheikh Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan thanked President Dissanayake for Sri Lanka\u2019s expression of solidarity and its supportive position.\n\nBoth leaders emphasised the need to immediately de-escalate military tensions in order to prevent the conflict from expanding further and to limit potential repercussions for regional and global security.\n\nCommenting separately on the discussion, President Dissanayake said he had conveyed condolences and solidarity to the UAE following the recent attacks.\n\n\u201cI telephoned His Highness @MohamedBinZayed, President of the UAE, to express my sadness over the recent attacks suffered by the UAE. I assured him of Sri Lanka\u2019s solidarity while condemning all forms of violence and terrorism. Sri Lanka stands firmly with the UAE and is ready to assist in any way it can,\u201d he said in a statement posted on the social media platform \u2018X.\u2019\n\nThe call comes amid heightened tensions in the Middle East following Iran\u2019s retaliatory strikes on US assets in the region."
