    "md5": "17fcb6947f375ed14adb273a88679bab",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1497,
    "chunk_text": "Following the impact of Cyclone Ditwah, DPL extended financial assistance to affected farmer communities in Kegalle, with a focus on families who experienced crop loss and property damage. Based on internal field assessments that considered the severity of impact and livelihood disruption, assistance was distributed among 22 affected farmers to support recovery and help restore their income sources.\n\nAs part of its education outreach initiatives, employee volunteers engaged with students with visual and hearing impairments at MO/Wellassa Subahagya Vidyalaya through drawing sessions and interactive games, creating a joyful and inclusive experience for the children. A drinking water system was installed and handed over to ensure safe and reliable access to clean water. Several items requested by the school were donated to support day-to-day needs and enhance their learning environment.\n\nThese initiatives reflect DPL\u2019s enduring commitment to social progress and national development,\u201d said Janadheera. \u201cAs the company reflects on five decades of growth, we continue to recognise that our success is inseparable from the well-being of the communities we serve and our larger family of employees and small-scale suppliers that make up our grassroot supply chains. Marking 50 years, Dipped Products PLC reaffirms its responsibility to contribute meaningfully to Sri Lanka\u2019s development, strengthening lives, supporting livelihoods, and creating lasting value across generations.\u201d"
  },
