    "chunk_size_bytes": 1291,
    "chunk_text": "US citizens in Sri Lanka advised to stay alert amid ME tensions\n\nThe United States Embassy in Colombo has urged American citizens in Sri Lanka to remain alert and enrol in the Smart Traveler Enrolment Program (STEP) to receive security updates in light of ongoing developments in the Middle East.\n\n\u201cWe encourage all American citizens to sign up for STEP at [http://step.state.gov](http://step.state.gov) to get the latest security updates from the nearest U.S. embassy or consulate,\u201d the embassy said in a message posted on its social media platforms.\n\n\u201cThe US Department of State has no higher priority than the safety and security of Americans worldwide.\u201d\n\nThe embassy noted that commercial travel routes which avoid transit through the Middle East are available for those planning to return to the United States. \u201cIf your travel plans have been affected and you wish to speak with a Consular Officer, walk-in hours are available Monday-Thursday, 1:00\u20132:00 p.m.\u201d\n\n\u201cFor urgent assistance or if you cannot visit during these hours, please contact the Embassy\u2019s American Citizen Services Unit +94-11-202-8500 or email us via U.S. Citizens Services Navigator. [https://tinyurl.com/ACS-Visa-Navigator](https://tinyurl.com/ACS-Visa-Navigator). (Colombo/Mar06/2026),\u201d it said."
