    "md5": "8c4b739613cdd7123fdee530fac850f9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1016,
    "chunk_text": "Two Sessions, One Xi\n\nChinese Two Sessions, the most consequential political gatherings in China, have drawn comparatively limited attention this year, overshadowed by escalating military operations in Iran conducted jointly by the United States and Israel following the decapitation of the country\u2019s head of state, Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei, just weeks after the violent removal of Venezuela\u2019s leadership. Trump\u2019s decapitation projects appear to continue and could extend to Russia and then China, creating one of the most dangerous precedents in modern political history, where, from the American point of view, success or failure remains uncertain.\n\nChina appears to be losing, one by one, its most reliable partners, exposing vulnerabilities in Beijing\u2019s global network that have long been suspected but are now increasingly tangible. Amid these international upheavals, Xi Jinping presided over the Two Sessions in Beijing, which had just begun at the time of writing and will continue until 11 March."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-07-islandlk-ade902f8",
    "num": "islandlk-ade902f8",
