    "chunk_text": "A subtle but transformative development noted during this year\u2019s Two Sessions is the repatriation of Chinese experts from Western institutions. Senior scientists, engineers, and economists who trained or worked in the United States, Europe, and Canada are increasingly returning to China, bringing expertise in artificial intelligence, biotechnology, and advanced manufacturing. These returnees are pivotal in accelerating China\u2019s technological self-reliance, ensuring that innovation is not merely imported but indigenously adapted and scaled.\n\nThe Two Sessions have laid out clear economic, social, and technological objectives for 2026. According to the government work report submitted to the legislature, China sets a growth target of 4.5 to 5 per cent for the year, alongside the creation of over 12 million urban jobs. Consumer price growth is projected at around two per cent, the deficit-to-GDP ratio at roughly four per cent, and personal income is expected to rise in step with overall growth. Grain output is targeted at 700 million metric tonnes, and carbon dioxide emissions per unit of GDP are to fall by approximately 3.8 per cent. Policymakers emphasize the expansion of elderly care services and the development of the silver economy in response to an ageing population."
