    "md5": "1c3f9c60fabec8ce2e1fb8210eb7b67f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1092,
    "chunk_text": "He is harsh about what he sees as Carpenter\u2019s racism, and asks how \u2018the daughter of someone who supported the abolition of slavery in the United States\u2019 could harbour such deep racial prejudice? But even she is more positive than otherwise about the beauties of the island, and also of its children, while he records the ecstasy of others, in particular Mark Twain who said he had spent the most enchanting day of his life in Ceylon, and loved everything \u2013 except the prim European clothes of girls marching out of a missionary school. He much preferred the boy with just a twine string round his waist, which he thought \u2018a pleasant contrast with the odious flummery in which the little Sunday-school dowdies were masquerading\u2019.\n\nAll in all a fascinating account of different perspectives on this country, and we must be grateful to the writer for having put it all so lovingly together.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
