    "chunk_size_bytes": 2006,
    "chunk_text": "SLT Group reports strong FY 2025 performance driven by cost savings and efficiency\n\nThe SLT Group recorded strong financial growth in the year ended December 31, 2025, driven by cost optimisation, reduced finance costs and steady expansion across its fixed and mobile segments.\n\nThe Group reported a 221% surge in Profit After Tax to Rs. 10 billion, up from Rs. 3.1 billion in 2024, supported by disciplined expense management and improving operational efficiency. Group revenue rose 3% to Rs. 114.2 billion, while operating profit grew 26.9% to Rs. 14.2 billion. Interest costs declined by 21% to Rs. 7.05 billion as debt levels were reduced.\n\nThe mobile subsidiary Mobitel (Sri Lanka) delivered exceptional performance, posting a PAT of Rs. 3.1 billion \u2014 a 2,123% increase year-on-year \u2014 supported by stronger data revenue, value-added services and enterprise solutions. Revenue grew 5% to Rs. 47.9 billion amid rising data consumption and subscriber growth.\n\nThe parent company Sri Lanka Telecom PLC also maintained steady growth, with broadband expansion, particularly fibre-to-the-home (FTTH) services, driving revenue. Operating profit rose 27% to Rs. 9.3 billion, supported by lower financing costs.\n\nChairman Dr. Mothilal de Silva said the performance reflected the Group\u2019s strategic focus on cost control and sustainable growth. He highlighted the company\u2019s role in restoring network infrastructure following Cyclone Ditwah, where more than 98% of damaged sites were recovered within a week.\n\nChief Executive Officer Riyaaz Rasheed said the Group was entering 2026 with renewed focus on innovation, customer engagement and network expansion. He noted that the acquisition of 5G spectrum and islandwide deployment would support Sri Lanka\u2019s digital transformation.\n\nThe Group said future plans would prioritise fibre expansion, subscriber growth and enterprise digital services.\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank Commemorates International Women\u2019s Day 2026 with Enhanced benefits for \u2018Vanitha Vasana\u2019"
