    "md5": "a499421892d37f770f9549c086dcb745",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1739,
    "chunk_text": "Mercedes-Benz Fashion Week  Sri Lanka announces three-year vision and strategic partner alignment\n\nFrom left: Sampath Bank Managing Director/Chief Executive Officer Sanjaya Gunawardana, DIMO Executive Director Rajeev Pandithage, AOD Founder and Chairperson Linda Speldewinde, and Colombo Hotels Senior Vice President and Cinnamon Life at City of Dreams General Manager Kamal Munasinghe\n\nCinnamon Life at City of Dreams, Sampath Bank Private Banking, and Wijeya Newspapers join a group of key strategic partners aligning with DIMO and AOD as Mercedes-Benz Fashion Week Sri Lanka charts growth through 2028\n\nMercedes-Benz Fashion Week Sri Lanka (MBFW Sri Lanka) has unveiled an ambitious three-year strategic roadmap through 2028, signalling strong institutional confidence in the country\u2019s fashion and creative economy. The announcement confirms key long-term partnerships and provides the market with forward visibility as the platform continues to position Colombo as an emerging creative capital in South Asia.\n\nThe multi-year calendar reinforces the platform\u2019s stability and international intent, enabling designers, buyers, media, and global collaborators to plan with greater confidence.\n\nMercedes-Benz Fashion Week Sri Lanka continues to be presented by AOD and powered by DIMO, a partnership that has steadily strengthened the platform\u2019s global credibility and operational scale.\n\nDIMO, the only Authorised agent for Mercedes-Benz in Sri Lanka, plays a pivotal role in connecting the local platform to the wider Mercedes-Benz Fashion Week ecosystem worldwide. The deepening collaboration between AOD and DIMO signals a shared long-term commitment to elevating Sri Lanka\u2019s fashion industry onto the regional and global stage."
  },
