    "chunk_text": "As the Official Banking Partner of Mercedes-Benz Fashion Week Sri Lanka, Sampath Bank Private Banking aligns with a shared vision centred on innovation, ambition, and the advancement of Sri Lanka\u2019s emerging luxury and lifestyle economy. In parallel with the growth of its Premier Banking proposition for a new generation of discerning clients, this partnership provides a considered platform to engage with the country\u2019s expanding creative and professional communities. The collaboration reflects the Bank\u2019s forward-looking approach, positioning Premier Banking not merely as a financial offering, but as a gateway to experiences that resonate with fashion, design, and modern lifestyle aspirations.\n\nStrengthening the platform\u2019s national reach, Wijeya Newspapers Ltd., has been appointed Official Exclusive Media Partner for Mercedes-Benz Fashion Week Sri Lanka.\n\nThis strategic media alignment further reinforces MBFW Sri Lanka\u2019s position as the country\u2019s most internationally connected fashion platform.\n\nWijeya Newspapers Ltd., has been a valued supporter of Mercedes-Benz Fashion Week Sri Lanka since its inception, playing an important role in amplifying the platform\u2019s national visibility and cultural relevance. As the Wijeya media network evolves into a new-age, fully integrated multimedia powerhouse, strengthening its digital, online, and next-generation content capabilities while continuing to enhance its strong print legacy, the partnership enters a new phase of strategic alignment.\n\nWith confirmed dates through 2028 and a strengthened coalition of strategic partners, Mercedes-Benz Fashion Week Sri Lanka is entering a new phase of structured growth.\n\nThe platform continues to evolve beyond the runway into a broader ecosystem spanning fashion, design, retail, tourism, and creative technology, supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s wider ambition to grow its creative economy and position Colombo firmly on the regional creative map."
