    "chunk_size_bytes": 935,
    "chunk_text": "Spain recalls Ambassador to Israel as diplomatic rift deepens\n\nSpain has withdrawn its Ambassador to Israel, according to an announcement published in the country\u2019s official State Gazette, signalling a further deterioration in diplomatic relations between the two countries.\n\nFollowing the decision, the Spanish Embassy in Israel will be headed by a charg\u00e9 d\u2019affaires rather than a full ambassador.\n\nMadrid has been among the EU members most critical of Israel\u2019s military operations in Gaza and has also voiced concern over the wider conflict involving the US, Israel, and Iran.\n\nRelations between Spain and Israel have strained in recent months, particularly after Spain formally recognised a Palestinian State and called for stronger international action over the Gaza conflict.\n\nThe latest step reflects Spain\u2019s continuing criticism of Israel\u2019s military campaign and the broader escalation of tensions in the Middle East."
  },
