    "md5": "9ccad94d559b8ae565fa38af0c29d737",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 738,
    "chunk_text": "Three commercial vessels attacked near Strait of Hormuz\n\nThree commercial ships have been attacked in the Gulf near the Strait of Hormuz, with one vessel catching fire, according to international media reports citing AFP.\n\nThe incidents occurred close to the strategic waterway that links the Persian Gulf with global shipping lanes and serves as one of the world\u2019s most critical routes for oil and gas transport.\n\nReports said one of the vessels was set ablaze during the attack, while two other ships were also struck in the same incident.\n\nThe developments have heightened concerns over the security of maritime traffic in the Strait of Hormuz, a narrow passage through which roughly one-fifth of the world\u2019s oil supply is shipped."
  },
