    "md5": "ab6f48bbe9c15e8551795ce5e67a9ee2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1746,
    "chunk_text": "Link4 acquires Unifiedpost to strengthen Asia Pacific e-invoicing leadership\n\nLink4 has announced the acquisition of 100% of the shares of Unifiedpost Pte Ltd., from Banqup Group SA. The transaction includes all assets and customer relationships of the Singapore-based e-Invoicing provider.\n\nThe acquisition reinforces Link4\u2019s position as a growing regional leader in e-Invoicing across Asia-Pacific and strengthens its presence within Singapore\u2019s InvoiceNow network.\n\nUnifiedpost Pte Ltd., has operated as an accredited provider within Singapore\u2019s InvoiceNow framework. Link4 will continue to support all existing customers and ensure a smooth transition of services. As part of the integration, the Access Point accreditation of Unifiedpost Group and the IRSP accreditation of Unifiedpost Pte Ltd., with IMDA will terminate effective 31 March 2026, with customers continuing under Link4\u2019s established accreditation.\n\nLink4 CEO and Co-Founder Robin Sands said: \u201cSingapore is a strategic digital trade hub in Asia. This acquisition reflects our confidence in the long-term growth of e-Invoicing across the region. Governments throughout Asia-Pacific are accelerating digital mandate programs, and Link4 is building the infrastructure to support businesses in every market adopting these frameworks.\u201d\n\nFounded in 2016, Link4 has expanded from Australia into multiple Asia-Pacific jurisdictions and now supports thousands of organisations across the region. The company focuses exclusively on compliant, scalable e-Invoicing solutions integrated with leading ERP systems.\n\nThe acquisition strengthens Link4\u2019s: Singapore market position; Recurring revenue base; Regional customer footprint and Long-term mandate-driven growth strategy."
  },
