    "chunk_size_bytes": 782,
    "chunk_text": "Melstacorp trims stake in DCSL with Rs. 118 m share sale\n\nMelstacorp PLC yesterday said it has marginally reduced its stake in Distilleries Company of Sri Lanka PLC (DCSL) following the sale of two million shares.\n\nIt divested the shares on 11 March from its existing holding of 4,250,264,664 shares in DCSL.\n\nThe shares were sold at Rs. 59 each, placing the total value of the transaction at approximately Rs. 118 million.\n\nDCSL is the flagship spirits manufacturing subsidiary of the Melstacorp Group and remains one of the group\u2019s largest investments. Despite the divestment, Melstacorp continues to retain overwhelming control of the company with a holding exceeding 92%.\n\nFollowing the transaction, Melstacorp\u2019s shareholding in DCSL declined slightly from 92.40% to 92.35%."
