    "description": "Trump announces $ 300 b refinery deal with India\u2019s Reliance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Trump-announces-300-b-refinery-deal-with-India-s-Reliance/34-789501",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1773367706.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-13-dailyftlk-6e844210-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d12fb1c452c419cb8c43331b3b4905ac",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1248,
    "chunk_text": "Trump announces $ 300 b refinery deal with India\u2019s Reliance\n\nUS President Donald Trump on Tuesday announced plans for what he described as the first oil refinery to be built in the US in 50 years, backed by investments from Indian conglomerate Reliance Industries.\n\nIn a statement posted on the Truth Social platform, Trump said the project represents a $ 300 billion investment and thanked Reliance Industries for its participation.\n\nThe refinery will be located at the Port of Brownsville in Texas and is designed to process 100% US-produced shale oil. The project is being developed by America First Refining.\n\nReliance Industries, controlled by Indian billionaire Mukesh Ambani, operates the world\u2019s largest oil refining complex in Jamnagar, India, and has a market capitalisation of about $ 206 billion according to LSEG Data.\n\nThe announcement comes at a time when global oil markets are experiencing heightened volatility due to the escalating conflict in the Middle East.\n\nAccording to project estimates, the refinery is expected to process around 1.2 billion barrels of US light shale oil valued at about $ 125 billion and produce approximately 50 billion gallons of refined petroleum products with an estimated value of $ 175 billion."
  },
