    "md5": "8b2bfdf5fdd7cae0ac0c1d95d613840d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1916,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Institute of Information Technology raises the bar for academic excellence\n\nThe Sri Lanka Institute of Information Technology (SLIIT), the country\u2019s leading provider of non-state higher education, successfully concluded its March 2026 Convocation. The event recognized over 800 graduates and postgraduates whose achievements represent the highest standards of scholarship, leadership, and community engagement.\n\nThe convocation took place over two days at the SLIIT Malabe Campus Main Auditorium. On 3-4 March, students, their families, faculty, and alumni gathered to recognize and applaud the hard work, talent, and perseverance of each graduate who walked across the stage to receive their certificate.\n\nA new cohort of students leaves SLIIT with qualifications and specializations that are flexible, accessible, and relevant to a hyper competitive job market. The Vice Chancellor\u2019s address called on these graduates to leave university knowing they are forward thinkers who can enact change in their own lives, professions, and in their communities.\n\nProf. Elizabeth Croft, Vice-President Academic and Provost, University of Victoria Canada (UVic) was the Chief Guest on day one, with Associate Vice President for Global Engagement at UVic, Dr. A. R. Elangovan, also in attendance. Dr. Christian Matthews, Assistant Faculty Pro-Vice Chancellor at Liverpool John Moores University made his Chief Guest address virtually.\n\nIndustry partners representing Bank of Ceylon, Dialog Axiata, Genetech, IFS R&D International, Scybers, Six Sigma Management Institute, Suchith Mohotti Associates, and Walkers CML also joined the distinguished gathering.\n\nThe 2026 convocation was yet another milestone in a remarkable journey begun over 25 years ago. Since 1999, SLIIT has provided rigorous and innovative training to a growing population of young people, who choose SLIIT for its impactful student experience."
