    "md5": "f9a5750516f3e4c10cc9472e02ca380b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1521,
    "chunk_text": "Alumex PLC powers  innovation as official material  sponsor of \u2018Unleashed 2026\u2019\n\nAlumex PLC, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading aluminium extrusion manufacturer, was proud to be the official material sponsor for the event, \u2018Unleashed 2026\u2019 \u2013 the launch of FALCON E1, a next-generation electric racing car designed and built entirely by students of the University of Moratuwa.\n\nThe event which was held recently at the university, marked a milestone in Sri Lanka\u2019s engineering innovation landscape. Developed by the university\u2019s Team Falcon Racing, the FALCON E1 is a completely new electric race car built from the ground up, using advanced engineering design, precision manufacturing techniques and cutting-edge electric vehicle technologies.\n\nAs the official material sponsor, Alumex provided critical aluminium inputs that formed part of the vehicle\u2019s construction, including aluminium components weighing approximately 650 kilograms. The company also extended specialised anodising services for machined components, enhancing the power to weight ratio, while maintaining structural integrity required under racing conditions.\n\nAlumex has consistently supported Sri Lanka\u2019s student engineering innovation ecosystem and took particular pride in contributing to this project. Notably, this marks the third consecutive occasion on which Alumex has supported the development of Sri Lanka\u2019s electric racing vehicles, reinforcing its commitment to nurturing engineering excellence and sustainable mobility innovation."
  },
