    "chunk_size_bytes": 1929,
    "chunk_text": "SLFPA unveils 23rd edition of Profood Propack & Agbiz Knowledge Hub\n\nThe highly anticipated event on Sri Lanka\u2019s food industry calendar, Profood Propack & Agbiz Knowledge Hub 2026, organised by the Sri Lanka Food Processors Association (SLFPA) in partnership with Lanka Exhibition and Conference Services (LECS), is scheduled to take place from 21 to 23 August 2026 at BMICH, Colombo.\n\nThe announcement was made during the award ceremony of the 22nd edition, held on 10 March at Cinnamon Grand Colombo, where industry leaders and key stakeholders convened to celebrate excellence within the sector. The event provided an ideal platform for SLFPA to outline its vision for the future, unveiling plans for a more expansive and impactful edition in the year ahead.\n\nEndorsed by the Industries Ministry, the National Agribusiness Council, and the Institute of Food Science and Technology Sri Lanka (IFSTSL), Profood Propack 2026 has served as SLFPA\u2019s flagship platform for over 25 years, advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s food sector and supporting wider economic growth. The exhibition unites leaders from agriculture, food processing, packaging, and allied industries, fostering innovation, knowledge exchange, and strategic collaboration.\n\nSpeaking at the event, SLFPA President Thusith Wijesinghe said: \u201cProfood Propack & Agbiz Knowledge Hub 2026 continues to set the benchmark for Sri Lanka\u2019s food industry. By bringing together key local and international stakeholders, the exhibition fosters innovation, collaboration, and growth across the sector.\u201d\n\nProfood Propack connects distributors, manufacturers, suppliers, and industry professionals, showcasing the latest advancements in food and beverage production, processing, packaging machinery, and hospitality sector. The exhibition also highlights operational efficiency, smart manufacturing, and sustainable practices to meet the evolving needs of the modern food industry."
  },
