    "md5": "27cbbbfc13e107ad24be69c7876c9bec",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1385,
    "chunk_text": "President reviews progress on reform of 124 non-commercial State institutions\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake on Tuesday convened the Officials\u2019 Committee to review progress on the implementation of the Cabinet decision concerning 124 non-commercial State institutions.\n\nThe meeting, held at the Presidential Secretariat, assessed the implementation of the Cabinet of Ministers-approved decision taken on 17 March 2025 to rationalise non-commercial State institutions and improve public sector efficiency.\n\nThe said Cabinet decision had directed a comprehensive review of these non-commercial State institutions under nine categories, citing concerns over outdated operations, inadequacy of vested powers, overlap of functions, and the potential for certain roles to be more efficiently handled by the private sector.\n\nAccording to the President\u2019s Media Division, the meeting focused on the current implementation status, challenges faced by specific State institutions, and measures needed to address them.\n\nThe responsibility of reporting the progress of implementing these decisions to the Cabinet of Ministers on a quarterly basis has also been entrusted to the above Officials\u2019 Committee.\n\nThe Officials\u2019 Committee, chaired by Secretary to the Prime Minister Pradeep Saputhanthri, is tasked with supervising the reforms and reporting progress quarterly to the Cabinet."
