    "md5": "1983280d34fc0be18abe5875159e3128",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1575,
    "chunk_text": "One Heart, One Voice \u2013 A choral concert presented by the Lanka Alzheimer\u2019s Foundation\n\nMusic, friendship and a shared sense of purpose come together this month when the Senior Community Choir of Soul Sounds Academy is featured in \u201cOne Heart, One Voice,\u201d a special choral concert presented by the Lanka Alzheimer\u2019s Foundation, directed by Soundarie David Rodrigo. The performance will take place on 22 March 2026 at the Lionel Wendt Theatre, bringing together voices and hearts for a cause that touches countless families.\n\nAt Soul Sounds Academy, Monday and Thursday rehearsals are far from quiet affairs. The room hums with animated chatter as choir members gather, greeting one another warmly before settling down to rehearse. Soon the sound of music fills the space as altos, sopranos and descants practise their parts with enthusiasm, building toward what promises to be an uplifting evening of song.\n\nThe repertoire is a delightful journey through some of Broadway\u2019s most beloved musicals, featuring numbers from The Sound of Music, My Fair Lady, South Pacific, Mary Poppins, Oklahoma! and Evita, along with several other favourites. Adding to the evening\u2019s appeal will be a guest appearance by Soul Sounds, Sri Lanka\u2019s premier female vocal ensemble.\n\nPresiding over this lively musical gathering is Soundarie David Rodrigo, the Music Director of Soul Sounds Academy. Elegant as always in a beautiful saree, she enters the rehearsal room to warm smiles and eager anticipation. Under her gentle but assured guidance, voices blend and harmonies take shape."
  },
