    "chunk_size_bytes": 1920,
    "chunk_text": "Presiding over this lively musical gathering is Soundarie David Rodrigo, the Music Director of Soul Sounds Academy. Elegant as always in a beautiful saree, she enters the rehearsal room to warm smiles and eager anticipation. Under her gentle but assured guidance, voices blend and harmonies take shape.\n\nAdding a touch of theatrical discipline to rehearsals is  Jerome de Silva, the accomplished Artistic Director. Known for his strict standards and sharp attention to detail, Jerome keeps the choir firmly on track. He is not above delivering a well-aimed reprimand when lyrics falter or focus drifts, but the choir takes his tough love in good humour as they strive to meet the high standards he set.\n\nBeyond the music, \u201cOne Heart, One Voice\u201d carries a deeper purpose. The concert coincides with the 25th anniversary of the Lanka Alzheimer\u2019s Foundation, an organisation dedicated to improving the quality of life for those living with Alzheimer\u2019s disease and related dementias, as well as their families and caregivers.\n\nAlzheimer\u2019s disease is a condition that gradually affects memory, thinking and behaviour, and its impact reaches far beyond the individual diagnosed. Many families know the pain of watching a loved one slowly lose memories and independence. Fortunately, greater awareness today has helped replace stigma with compassion and understanding.\n\nThe Lanka Alzheimer\u2019s Foundation was founded by Lorraine Yu and Tami Tamitigama, whose vision was to provide support, education and care for families affected by dementia. From modest beginnings, the organisation has grown steadily over the past quarter century.\n\nToday, under the skilful leadership of Professor Shehan Williams, the Foundation continues to expand its work. Its centre in Colombo 10 offers diagnostic services, therapeutic activities and guidance, providing much-needed support to families navigating the challenges of dementia."
