    "chunk_text": "In November 2003, at an event to mark the 20th anniversary of the National Endowment for Democracy, George W Bush assured his credulous nation that \u201cA new regime in Iraq would serve as a dramatic and inspiring example of freedom for other nations in the region.\u201d Knowingly or unknowingly, he was echoing Bibi Netanyahu\u2019s blithe and misleading words to the US Congress during a hearing on Iraq, \u201cA war on Iraq is a good choice, the right choice\u2026 A nuclear-armed Saddam would place the security of our entire world at risk\u2026 If you take out Saddam, Saddam\u2019s regime, I guarantee you that it will have positive reverberations in the region\u201d (https://www.vox.com/2015/2/26/8114221/netanyahu-iraq-2002).\n\nAccording to a report by France 24, Israel drones are spraying herbicides on crops and even fruit trees in the buffer zone between Israel and Syria, destroying them (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lyp9Xfess3Q). This is despite the pro-Israeli nature of Syria\u2019s new regime. Clearly anarchy and chaos in the region is what Israel is after. A long war in Iran or \u2013 ideally \u2013 the fragmentation of Iran resulting in a series of civil wars would suit Israel\u2019s purpose perfectly."
