    "chunk_text": "JKH sells off Cinnamon Citadel for Rs. 2.8 bn. ahead of opening new Kandy property\n\nJohn Keells Hotels PLC, a member of the JKH group, has sold its decades owned riverfront Kandy property for nearly Rs. 2.8 billion to Lavendish Leisure, the hospitality arm of the Dedigama Group in the context of commencement of operations their new hotel, Kandy Myst by Cinnamon, in the hill capital.\n\nJKH said in a stock exchange filing that the group was divesting its total shareholding of 98.39% Kandy Walk Inn Ltd. which is the owning company of the Cinnamon Citadel hotel, one of the older properties owned by the group. It will continue, in agreement with the Acquirer, to manage the hotel under the Cinnamon Hotels and Resorts brand for a minimum period of 12 months subject to review thereafter.\n\nEstablished in 1950, the Dedigama group\u2019s business reach spans financial services, jewellery, gem and jewel exports, hospitality, commercial real estate and property development, plantations and international joint ventures across various verticals.\n\nJKH said\u201dthe divestment is aligned with the asset light strategy of the hotels business and the commencement of operations of Kandy Myst by Cinnamon, the operating entity of which is 40% owned by the Company. Further, proceeds from the divestment will facilitate the optimum allocation of capital towards upgrading the hotel portfolio of the Company in line with the positioning and future outlook of these properties,\u201d the JKH filing said.\n\nThe transaction is expected to be completed by March 31, 2026.\n\nWedgefishes and Guitarfishes in Sri Lanka: The Urgent Need for Conservation\n\nCaltex Abimani Strengthens the Next Generation of Women in STEM\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
