    "chunk_text": "The lecture at the Sapumal Foundation traces his interest in art to his early life in Koggala and his immersion in art history. It assesses his critiques of scholars of Sri Lankan and South Asian art. Finally, it appraises his reputation as a leading literary figure against the backdrop of cultural modernism in Sri Lanka and in South Asia.\n\nThese explored diverse aspects to Wickramasinghe\u2019s life, work, and thought, focusing on views on subjects like culture, society, politics, and anthropology. Devapriya is also involved in a major study of Martin Wickramasinghe, slated for review and publication this year. Incorporating primary archive material and interviews with scholars and acquaintances of Wickramasinghe, the book marks a culmination to nearly two years of research into one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most iconic literary and cultural figures.\n\nFor more information on the lecture, contact Uditha via email at or WhatsApp and phone at (+94)716419646.\n\nOne Heart, One Voice \u2013 A choral concert presented by the Lanka Alzheimer\u2019s Foundation\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
