    "chunk_size_bytes": 1683,
    "chunk_text": "HP Outlines Five-Pillar Strategy to Enable Digital Inclusion in Sri Lanka\n\nHP has reinforced its long-term commitment to Sri Lanka\u2019s digital transformation, unveiling a five-pillar strategic framework focused on expanding access and accelerating AI-led growth across the country.\n\nAt a media roundtable led by Ipsita Dasgupta, SVP and MD for HP India, Sri Lanka, and Bangladesh, the company highlighted Sri Lanka as one of its fastest-growing markets in the region, with approximately 27% market share as of Q4 2025.\n\nThe first pillar aims to put a PC in every child\u2019s hand, bridging the digital divide through AI-driven, language-enabled devices for personalized learning. The second focuses on empowering MSMEs through on-device AI to improve efficiency, security, and productivity.\n\nHP\u2019s third pillar involves partnering with local enterprises on technology modernization and workforce strategies. The fourth explores government collaborations in healthcare, education, and skilling through proof-of-concept initiatives.\n\nThe fifth pillar positions emerging markets at the centre of HP\u2019s growth strategy, developing tailored solutions to unlock the next wave of digital users.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka reflects the ambition, resilience, and digital potential we see across emerging economies,\u201d said Dasgupta, reaffirming HP\u2019s commitment to enabling inclusive growth through technology access and innovation.\n\nAgrovista Plantation plants 250,000 trees under \u2018One Million Trees\u2019 drive\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
