    "chunk_text": "Agrovista Plantation plants 250,000 trees under \u2018One Million Trees\u2019 drive\n\nAgrovista Plantation has announced significant early progress in its \u201cOne Million Trees for the Motherland by 2030\u201d initiative, surpassing 250,000 trees planted since the program launched in 2024.\n\nThe ambitious environmental drive aims to plant one million trees across Sri Lanka by 2030 as part of the company\u2019s corporate social responsibility commitment. It focuses heavily on engaging school children, providing resources and guidance for students to plant, nurture, and protect trees.\n\nBy involving young people in conservation activities, Agrovista seeks to instill lifelong environmental awareness and responsibility. The broader vision encompasses climate resilience, biodiversity conservation, and expanding green landscapes nationwide.\n\nThe company invites individuals, organizations, and schools to support the mission through participation, plant donations, or partnerships.\n\n\u201cThrough collective effort, we can build a greener Sri Lanka for future generations,\u201d a company spokesperson said.\n\nComBank and Ideal Motors join forces for Mahindra XUV 3XO leasing deal\n\nHP Outlines Five-Pillar Strategy to Enable Digital Inclusion in Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
