    "chunk_id": "2026-03-16-dailyftlk-cef7e95c-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "93a4688c2672b3737af0e5f48f362542",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 943,
    "chunk_text": "Iran allows several Indian vessels safe passage through Strait of Hormuz: Envoy\n\nIran has granted limited safe passage to several Indian vessels through the Strait of Hormuz, Tehranian Ambassador to India Mohammad Fathali said, without specifying how many ships were allowed to pass.\n\nFathali made the remarks while speaking at broadcaster India Today\u2019s conclave in New Delhi. The move marks a rare exception to the broader restriction on maritime traffic through the waterway, which Iran has largely halted amid the ongoing conflict with the US and Israel.\n\nTwo Indian-flagged tankers carrying liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) bound for ports in the country\u2019s west crossed the Strait of Hormuz, the South Asian country\u2019s Ports, Shipping and Waterways Ministry said. \u201cThey crossed the Strait of Hormuz early morning safely and are en route to India,\u201d Ministry Special Secretary Rajesh Kumar Sinha said at a news conference in New Delhi."
  },
