    "chunk_size_bytes": 1064,
    "chunk_text": "Amirthalingam who was the Sri Lankan leader of the opposition in 1977-83 was a TULF National list MP when he was brutally assassinated by the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam (LTTE) on July 13th 1989. Amirthalingam and his spouse Mangaiyarkkarasi were an inseparable duo in personal and public life.\n\nAgainst that backdrop, it is indeed correct that media reports should emphasise that Mangaiyarkkarasi was the wife of Amirthalingam. Had it not been for her marriage to him, Mangaiyarkkarasi may have never entered the political sphere in the way she did. Nevertheless what must be realised is that Mangaiyarkkarasi Amirthalingam was a political personality in her own right.\n\nAlthough she walked willingly with her husband on his political path and talked his political talk, Mangaiyarkkarasi did not bask in reflected glory. She herself had an impressive charisma of her own that went down well with the masses in the not so distant past. Mangaiyarkkarasi had a refreshingly independent mind of her own and exerted much influence politically in the bygone years."
