    "chunk_size_bytes": 1121,
    "chunk_text": "Maldives Airport Company gets UL\u2019s 3-year Mal\u00e9 ground handling deal at $ 16.19 m\n\nMaldives Airport Company Ltd., has won the contract to provide ground handling services to the national carrier\u2014SriLankan Airlines in Mal\u00e9 International Airport, Maldives for three years.\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers on Monday approved the proposal by the Ports and Civil Aviation Minister to award the contract for three years from 1 April 2026.\n\nThe existing contract for providing ground handling services at Mal\u00e9 Airport is scheduled to expire on 31 March 2026.\n\nAddressing the weekly post-Cabinet meeting media briefing yesterday, Cabinet Spokesman and Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa disclosed the estimated value of the contract for Mal\u00e9 Airport ground handling services is $ 16.19 million.\n\n\u201cA proposal has been obtained from the sole service provider that provides the ground handling services at the said airport for the provision of these services. Based on the recommendations of the Higher-Level Standing Procurement Committee, it recommended awarding the relevant contract to Maldives Airport Company Ltd.,\u201d he added."
